{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-6810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/assets/4969bf3cea8290c76e79419ed0160a8c1f92d7415250305df56eb8128ad15cf4.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx={t}^{4}+t-1,\\,y={t}^{3},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4{t}^{3}+1,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{4{t}^{3}+1}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=-1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{3(-1)^{2}}{4(-1)^{3}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(-4)+1} \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fefba3e4315793a3c9f4c55cdb72affd02ac452bfbfde064deb695ad39fd6834"} {"question" "q-6810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{2}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=({t}^{3}-1){e}^{t},\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=({t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1){e}^{t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{({t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1){e}^{t}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=0$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{({0}^{3}+3\\cdot {0}^{2}-1){e}^{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1)}{(-1)\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fefba3e4315793a3c9f4c55cdb72affd02ac452bfbfde064deb695ad39fd6834"} {"question" "q-6812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{1}{2e}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{1}{3e}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{e}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{t},\\,y=8t-3,\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=4.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}{|}_{t\\,=\\,4}=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=8.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{8}{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}})}=16\\sqrt{t}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=4$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}{|}_{t\\,=\\,4} & =16\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =16(2) \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fefba3e4315793a3c9f4c55cdb72affd02ac452bfbfde064deb695ad39fd6834"} {"question" "q-353346" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353346" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-20990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/assets/5855e92b04ffbf8447d32c7edb190cd16046a13e8808e6ffaade1f59e414c869.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=2t{e}^{t},\\,y={t}^{2}+2t,\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-20990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{e}^{t}(t+1),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t+2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2t+2}{2{e}^{t}(t+1)}=\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-20990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fefba3e4315793a3c9f4c55cdb72affd02ac452bfbfde064deb695ad39fd6834"} {"question" "q-20990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-20990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2e}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3e}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{e}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{e}^{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-20990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{e}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/assets/5d4abbff66a225f92a8e4f5d30fb86b0b8e205b8a047ed3ed9d5af7290ac89c6.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={t}^{5}-2t,\\,y=1-{t}^{3},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}-2,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-3{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{-3{t}^{2}}{5{t}^{4}-2}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=-1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-3(-1)^{2}}{5(-1)^{4}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{5-2} \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fefba3e4315793a3c9f4c55cdb72affd02ac452bfbfde064deb695ad39fd6834"} {"question" "q-6848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/assets/1739317bf1b1c567f74dccf5b24a1b1dde8eb101d20ceec9652f604dc6f84543.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nshown above, calculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t=\\pi /6} & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fefba3e4315793a3c9f4c55cdb72affd02ac452bfbfde064deb695ad39fd6834"} {"question" "q-6808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-6808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\,\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/assets/35c62ccf48c4d0a49729da04b443cb94d112e673e0c24e7784d22f48eaabf8f7.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nshown above, calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$m=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,\\pi /3} & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fefba3e4315793a3c9f4c55cdb72affd02ac452bfbfde064deb695ad39fd6834"} {"question" "q-353351" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353351" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3\\sqrt{3}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-348304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/assets/7ae65c873838ede4cce89c953ff2654fa1e58e65fdc87896c8ba85bbf947be20.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nshown above, calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-348304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t}{(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,\\pi /4} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-348304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fefba3e4315793a3c9f4c55cdb72affd02ac452bfbfde064deb695ad39fd6834"} {"question" "q-348304" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-348304" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/assets/abab926e465522d30b236577bf8a1654502807b864c9fed8a4cebb84efffd3a2.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nshown above, calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$m=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,\\pi /4} & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fefba3e4315793a3c9f4c55cdb72affd02ac452bfbfde064deb695ad39fd6834"} {"question" "q-353350" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-353350" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-363490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{3/t},\\,y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}},\\,0<t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$m=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-363490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{3/t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}})}{(-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{3/t})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}\\,{e}^{3/t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,1} & =\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3({1}^{2}+4)^{3/2}\\,{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3(5)^{3/2}\\,{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15\\sqrt{5}\\,{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{75{e}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-363490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fefba3e4315793a3c9f4c55cdb72affd02ac452bfbfde064deb695ad39fd6834"} {"question" "q-363490" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "q-363490" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{15e^3\\sqrt{5}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/state.json" "file_sha256" "415efed87ec4cbe48fb8d78ebb976f3f46b9b6623a1814cc5bc3fab2127a17ab"} {"question" "e-595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\cos{t}, \\quad y=\\sin{t}, \\qquad  0\\leq t<2\\pi,\n$$\n\n calculate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/assets/2ec95dd061fa6b7f09c9f899a1f6483b4ea7d5127372ddd6eefb74d6ed10c14c.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/example-595.json" "file_sha256" "8c39aebb568a15162b22872776957f0d74a5a013b63be8762b419fc14116a933"} {"question" "e-595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = -\\sin{t}, \\qquad y'(t)=\\cos{t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\cos t}{-\\sin t} = -\\cot t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/example-595.json" "file_sha256" "8c39aebb568a15162b22872776957f0d74a5a013b63be8762b419fc14116a933"} {"question" "e-596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=te^t, \\quad y=e^{-t}, \\qquad -\\infty < t <\\infty,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/example-596.json" "file_sha256" "5ead9feed558af36cfab5e26350d6eb6d316dbc075639f9ce0d708cb9a858860"} {"question" "e-596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = e^t + te^t = (1+t)e^t, \\qquad y'(t)=-e^{-t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-{e}^{-t}}{(1+t){e}^{t}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1+t){e}^{2t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t=1} & =-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2(1)}(1+1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077511/example-596.json" "file_sha256" "5ead9feed558af36cfab5e26350d6eb6d316dbc075639f9ce0d708cb9a858860"}] "usage" {"e-595" [] "q-6808" [] "e-596" []} "basis" 2805 "retractions" [[17592186083825 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/798/Source/Images/q-6808.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve\n$x = 4\\cos t, y = 3\\sin 2t, 0 \\le t < 2\\pi $,\nshown above, calculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t = \\frac{\\pi }{6}$."] [17592186082971 :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n$x=\\cos{t}, \\quad y=\\sin{t}, \\qquad 0\\leq t<2\\pi$, calculate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/798/Source/Images/0f8bfc82b98e63e586e9d2e96d1acc5d.png)"] [17592186082971 :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y$, we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = -\\sin{t}, \\qquad y'(t)=\\cos{t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\cos t}{-\\sin t} = -\\cot t\n$$"] [17592186082972 :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n$x=te^t, \\quad y=e^{-t}, \\qquad -\\infty < t <\\infty$,\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1$."] [17592186082972 :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y$, we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = e^t + te^t = (1+t)e^t, \\qquad y'(t)=-e^{-t}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\frac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} x} & = \\frac{- {e}^{- t}}{( 1 + t ) {e}^{t}} \\\\  & = - \\frac{1}{( 1 + t ) {e}^{2 t}} .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1$, the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\frac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} x} |}_{t = 1} & = - \\frac{1}{{e}^{2 ( 1 )} ( 1 + 1 )} \\\\  & = - \\frac{1}{2 {e}^{2}} .\\end{array}$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186082317 17592186082318 17592186082319 17592186082320 17592186082321] "immutable_fields" [[17592186082316 :answer-field/correct] [17592186082316 :answer-field/id] [17592186082316 :answer-field/key] [17592186082316 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
